+/-- **A gain is given on a rising requirement by a supported formation.** With balance across the
+step at each condition the formation requires, and whatever gives to such a condition there
+supported, it cannot be refuted that a gain of support by a formation whose requirements do not
+loosen is given, on a condition it requires that rises across the step, by a supported formation
+taking part. The double negation locates the condition that rose. -/
+theorem gain_given_by_supported_at {t : Nat} {f : F}
+    (balances : ∀ c, W.requires t f c → L.BalancesOn W [c] t)
+    (givers : ∀ c, W.requires t f c → L.GiversSupported W t c) (gains : W.GainsSupport t f)
+    (unloosened : W.Unloosened t f) :
+    ¬ ¬ ∃ c g, W.requires t f c ∧ W.Rises t c ∧ g ∈ L.present t ∧ 0 < L.give t g c ∧
+      W.Supported t g :=
+  fun none => gains.rises unloosened fun c requires rises =>
+    match rise_given_by_supported_at (balances c requires) (givers c requires) rises with
+    | ⟨g, mem, gives, supported⟩ => none ⟨c, g, requires, rises, mem, gives, supported⟩
+
